--- body ---
## Source
0216 dogfood migration, 2026-06-03. Two of the six migrated stores
(cadens: 29 files, Climate_finance: 7 files) needed the same one-off
Python script after `erg migrate` ran clean -- the legacy pattern is
common enough to absorb into migrate itself.

## Context
`%erg v1`-era stores wrote log entries as a timestamped line followed by
free-form block content: indented wrap continuations, unindented prose
paragraphs, numbered lists, blank-line-separated paragraphs -- even
whole review documents. They also wrote date-only stamps
(`2026-04-23 claude ...` without `THH:MMZ`). All of these are
malformed-log-line violations under %erg 0.1, and migrate currently
leaves them: a store can exit `erg migrate` still failing validation.

That breaks migrate's implicit contract ("after migration, erg validate
will reject any REMAINING legacy lines" reads as: format legacies are
gone). It also defeats the per-file pre-commit validate on any repo
that installs hooks after migrating.

## Fix
Two new idempotent migrate rules, same spirit as the interior-blank
sweep (accept on read, autofix on write), applied inside the log
section only:

1. Fold: any line that does not start with a `YYYY-MM-DD` timestamp is
   joined (single-space, stripped) onto the preceding entry's line.
   Blank lines between an entry and its continuation content are
   dropped. Content before the first timestamped entry is left
   untouched (still a violation -- it has no parent entry; do not guess).
2. Stamp: a leading `YYYY-MM-DD ` (date, no time) is rewritten to
   `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00Z ` -- the conventional date-only normalization.

Reference behaviour: the throwaway normalizer used in the 0216 run
(joined 29 cadens + 7 Climate_finance files; full corpus validate PASS
after). Content is preserved verbatim modulo whitespace joins.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg migrate` on a fixture with wrapped details, unindented
      paragraphs, numbered lists, blank separators, and date-only
      stamps produces a store where `erg validate` passes on every file
- [ ] Idempotent: second run byte-identical (byte-compare, not counts)
- [ ] Orphan content before the first log entry is NOT folded and still
      reported by validate
- [ ] migrate summary line reports the two new rewrite counts
- [ ] make check passes

## Plan

### Verification of validator behavior (prerequisite for correctness)

Confirmed in src/go/erg.go lines 395-399: the log-section parser skips blank
lines (only appends when `trimmed != ""`). Rule 11 check (lines 493-498) also
skips blank `trimmed`. Therefore:
- Blank lines inside the log section are invisible to the validator — preserving
  them after folding satisfies "validate passes" (exit criterion 1).
- Non-blank lines that don't match `logLineRE` ARE flagged — orphan content
  before the first timestamped entry still fails (exit criterion 3 confirmed).

### Actions (numbered, file:line precise)

**1. src/go/ergspecv1.go — add two new regexes after logLineRE (line 100)**

Add adjacent to `logLineRE` with ABNF comments:

```go
// logEntryPrefixRE matches any log line that opens a new log entry:
// a line whose first 10 characters form a YYYY-MM-DD date. Used by
// foldLogLines to distinguish entry-openers from continuation lines.
//
// ABNF production:
//
//  log-entry-prefix := 4DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT
var logEntryPrefixRE = regexp.MustCompile(`^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}`)

// logDateOnlyRE matches a date-only log entry stamp (YYYY-MM-DD followed
// by a space, not a T). Used by foldLogLines to normalise legacy date-only
// stamps to YYYY-MM-DDT00:00Z form.
//
// ABNF production:
//
//  log-date-only := 4DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT "-" 2DIGIT SP
var logDateOnlyRE = regexp.MustCompile(`^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} `)
```

**2. src/go/migrate.go — add foldLogLines function (after migrateErgrc, ~line 447)**

Signature:
```go
func foldLogLines(log []string) (out []string, folded bool, stamped bool)
```

State machine (operates on the log-section slice only — preamble and body are
never passed in):
- Maintain: `cur string` (accumulated entry text), `pendingBlanks []string`,
  `seenFirstEntry bool`.
- For each `line` in `log`:
  - If `strings.TrimSpace(line) == ""`: append to `pendingBlanks`.
  - Else if `logEntryPrefixRE.MatchString(line)` (new entry opener):
    - Emit `cur` if non-empty (flush current accumulated entry).
    - Flush `pendingBlanks` to `out` (preserve inter-entry blanks).
    - Reset `pendingBlanks`.
    - Set `seenFirstEntry = true`.
    - If `logDateOnlyRE.MatchString(line)`: rewrite `line[:10] + "T00:00Z" +
      line[10:]` (line[10] is the space, so result is `...T00:00Z rest`);
      set `stamped = true`.
    - Start new entry: `cur = line`.
  - Else (non-blank, non-entry — continuation or orphan):
    - If `seenFirstEntry`: drop `pendingBlanks` (blanks between entry and its
      continuation are discarded); `cur += " " + strings.TrimSpace(line)`;
      set `folded = true`.
    - Else (orphan before first entry): flush `pendingBlanks`, emit `line`
      verbatim; `pendingBlanks = nil`.
- After loop: emit `cur` if non-empty; flush `pendingBlanks` (preserves
  trailing blank before `--- body ---`).

Idempotency argument: after one pass, every non-blank non-entry-opener line is
either folded onto its parent entry or emitted as an orphan. No such lines
remain, so a second pass has nothing to fold or stamp (date-only stamps already
rewritten to T00:00Z, which `logDateOnlyRE` does not match).

**3. src/go/migrate.go — wire foldLogLines into migrateFile (~line 363-365)**

After the `wasClosed` insertion block (after line 363), before `strings.Join`
(line 365):

```go
// Locate log and body separators in the (possibly rewritten) out slice.
logStartIdx := -1
bodyStartIdx := len(out)
for i, line := range out {
    if strings.TrimSpace(line) == separatorLog && logStartIdx < 0 {
        logStartIdx = i
    }
    if strings.TrimSpace(line) == separatorBody {
        bodyStartIdx = i
        break
    }
}
if logStartIdx >= 0 {
    logSlice := out[logStartIdx+1 : bodyStartIdx]
    folded, didFold, didStamp := foldLogLines(logSlice)
    if didFold || didStamp {
        // Build fresh slice to avoid append aliasing into out's backing array.
        newOut := make([]string, 0, len(out))
        newOut = append(newOut, out[:logStartIdx+1]...)
        newOut = append(newOut, folded...)
        newOut = append(newOut, out[bodyStartIdx:]...)
        out = newOut
        res.folded = didFold
        res.stamped = didStamp
    }
}
```

**4. src/go/migrate.go — extend migrateResult struct (~line 260-267)**

Add two fields:
```go
folded  bool // at least one log continuation line was folded onto its entry
stamped bool // at least one date-only log stamp was normalised to T00:00Z
```

**5. src/go/migrate.go — extend cmdMigrate counters and summary (~lines 68-119)**

Add counters:
```go
migratedFolded  := 0
migratedStamped := 0
```

In the per-file results block (~lines 91-106), add after the blanksSwept block:
```go
if res.folded {
    migratedFolded++
}
if res.stamped {
    migratedStamped++
