fmt.Printf("date-only stamp normalise: %d tickets\n", migratedStamped)
```

**6. src/go/migrate.go — extend helpMigrate (~lines 14-46)**

Add two rules to the bullet list in the `helpMigrate` constant, after the
"Interior blank lines" bullet:

```
  - Log continuation lines: any non-blank line in the log section that does
    not start with a YYYY-MM-DD timestamp is joined (single space, stripped)
    onto the preceding log entry. Blank lines between an entry and its
    continuation content are dropped. Content before the first timestamped
    entry is untouched.
  - Date-only log stamps: a leading 'YYYY-MM-DD ' (date, no T separator) is
    rewritten to 'YYYY-MM-DDT00:00Z '.
```

Also update the "After migration" sentence to mention these two new rules.

### Test plan (Go unit tests in src/go/migrate_test.go)

**Test A — TestFoldLogLines (pure-function unit test)**

Tests `foldLogLines` directly with a fixture containing:
- a full-timestamp entry with single-line detail (must survive unchanged)
- a date-only stamp entry (must be normalised to T00:00Z)
- a full-timestamp entry followed by: blank line, indented continuation,
  unindented continuation, numbered-list item — all joined in order with
  single spaces, blanks dropped
- blank lines between this entry and the next (preserved in output as
  inter-entry blanks)
- a second full-timestamp entry (clean — tests boundary)
- a trailing blank after the last entry (preserved — validates the
  "blank before --- body ---" invariant)

Assert:
- `folded == true`
- `stamped == true`
- exact `out` slice matches expected (in-order, single-space joins, orphan
  untouched, inter-entry blank preserved, trailing blank preserved)

Tautology check: a no-op implementation returns `(log, false, false)` —
it fails because `out` != expected folded content. A fold-only (no stamp)
implementation fails because date-only stamp not rewritten. A
global-fold (orphans too) fails because orphan line is altered.

**Test B — TestMigrateFileLogFold (integration test via migrateFile)**

Fixture content (full .erg file):
```
%erg 0.1
Title: T
Created: 2024-01-01
Author: test

--- log ---
2024-01-01 alice created
2024-01-02T10:00Z bob note This is a long note that wraps
onto this line
and this line too

2024-01-03T12:00Z carol note Short entry

--- body ---
body text
```

After migration:
```
%erg 0.1
Title: T
Created: 2024-01-01
Author: test

--- log ---
2024-01-01T00:00Z alice created
2024-01-02T10:00Z bob note This is a long note that wraps onto this line and this line too

2024-01-03T12:00Z carol note Short entry

--- body ---
body text
```

Assert:
- `res.folded == true`, `res.stamped == true`, `res.changed == true`
- file content byte-equals the expected string above

**Test C — TestMigrateFileIdempotentFold (idempotency test)**

Same fixture as Test B. Run `migrateFile` twice.
Assert:
- first run: `res.changed == true`
- read file bytes after first run → `after`
- second run: `res.changed == false`
- read file bytes after second run → bytes must equal `after` (byte-compare,
  not count check)

Tautology check: this fixture has blanks, wrapped lines, and date-only stamps.
A no-op implementation fails TestB's content assertion. TestC alone cannot be
passed by a no-op (TestB ensures the first-run content is correct, TestC
ensures the second run is a no-op on that correct content).

**Test D — TestMigrateFileOrphanUntouched**

Fixture with orphan text before the first timestamped entry:
```
%erg 0.1
Title: T
Created: 2024-01-01
Author: test

--- log ---
orphan line with no timestamp
2024-01-02T10:00Z alice note Real entry

--- body ---
```

Assert:
- `res.folded == false` (orphan is NOT folded)
- file content after migration still contains `orphan line with no timestamp`
  verbatim
- run `parseErg` on the migrated file; assert errs contains a malformed-log-line
  violation for the orphan (validator still flags it)

Tautology check: a global-fold implementation would fold orphan onto the next
entry (wrong) — this test would fail because the orphan disappears from the
file. The parseErg assertion confirms the orphan is still a violation.

### Fixture sketch

The idempotency fixture in TestC must include (all in one file to avoid a
combination explosion):
1. Trailing blank before `--- body ---` (preserving this is the CRITICAL invariant)
2. Inter-entry blank line (must survive folding)
3. Blank between an entry-opener and its continuation (must be dropped)
4. Multi-line continuation spanning both indented and unindented forms
5. Numbered-list item continuation
6. Date-only stamp entry
7. A full-timestamp entry with no continuation (regression guard — must be
   byte-identical after fold)

### Dependencies

None. Implementation is self-contained in `src/go/migrate.go` (new function +
wiring + bookkeeping) and `src/go/ergspecv1.go` (two new regexes). No new files
needed. No Blocked-by header required.

### Tautology-scan verdict

PASS — each test is designed to fail under a wrong or missing implementation:
- TestA catches wrong join order, missing stamp, global orphan fold, lost blanks
- TestB+C together: TestB catches wrong content; TestC catches blank accumulation
  on second run (the byte-compare, not marker-count pattern per memory entry)
- TestD catches treating orphans as foldable continuations
- The stamp idempotency guard (full timestamps in the same fixture) catches
  re-stamping bugs
